# Cloudflare Pages headers.
#
# ─── DELIBERATELY ABSENT: Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy ────────────────────────
# COEP + COOP would enable SharedArrayBuffer and multi-threaded WebAssembly, and
# it is tempting for an image-processing site. Do not add them here:
#
#   1. The jSquash codecs used on this site are single-threaded builds and do
#      not need SharedArrayBuffer.
#   2. Cross-origin isolation blocks third-party iframes that do not opt in,
#      which breaks Google AdSense completely.
#
# ─── DELIBERATELY ABSENT: Content-Security-Policy ─────────────────────────────
# AdSense loads from a wide and changing set of Google domains. A CSP that is
# even slightly wrong fails silently and stops ads rendering, with no error that
# points at the cause. Add one only after ads are live and verified, and test it
# on a preview deployment first.

# Hashed build assets never change content, so cache them forever. Astro emits
# every JS bundle and every WASM codec here with a content hash in the filename,
# so this one rule covers all of them.
#
# There used to be separate `/*.wasm` and `/*.js` rules as well. Both matched the
# same files as this rule, and Cloudflare Pages CONCATENATES matching rules, so
# the live response carried a doubled header:
#   Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable, public, max-age=…
# Harmless, but `/*.js` was also a trap: it matches any path depth, so any
# non-hashed script added at the root would silently become uncacheable-away for
# a year. If a JS or WASM file ever ships outside /_astro/, give it its own rule
# rather than reintroducing a global glob.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Fonts are self-hosted and their bytes never change for a given filename.
#
# RULE: if you ever swap a font file, RENAME it. There is no content hash in
# these paths, so overwriting one in place would strand the old bytes in every
# cache that already holds it — for a year.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# ─── Brand assets: revalidate, do not cache hard ─────────────────────────────
#
# Favicons, touch icons and Open Graph cards are GENERATED by
# scripts/make-assets.mjs, and their paths carry no content hash — /favicon.ico
# has to sit at /favicon.ico, and the manifest references icons by fixed path.
#
# These previously had `max-age=86400`. When the site was rebranded, the new
# favicon deployed correctly and the CDN kept serving the old one for the rest
# of the day, because a 24-hour cache is exactly what it was told to do. The
# bytes on disk were right and the site still showed the old mark — which is a
# very confusing thing to debug, and worse for an OG card, since social
# platforms cache those far longer than a browser does.
#
# `max-age=0, must-revalidate` keeps them in cache but forces a conditional
# request, so an unchanged file costs a ~100-byte 304 and a changed one appears
# immediately. These files are tiny and rarely re-fetched; correctness is worth
# far more here than the saved round trip.
/favicon.ico
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/favicon.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/favicon-16x16.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/favicon-32x32.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/favicon-48x48.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/apple-touch-icon.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/android-chrome-192x192.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/android-chrome-512x512.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/og/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  # This site never needs any of these. Denying them is a clear signal that a
  # tool asking you to drop private photos onto it is not reaching for hardware.
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
